Here is a JSON file `my_data.json`:

```json
{
    "people": [
        {
            "name": "John",
            "age": 30
        },
        {
            "name": "Jane",
            "age": 25
        }
    ]
}
```

Write a Python function `get_name_of_oldest_person` that reads the file `my_data.json` and returns the name of the oldest person. If there is a tie, return the name that appears first in the file. Assume the `age` values are integers and there is at least one person in the list.
